<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreign share of NZ govt securities rose in July.</title>
<headline>Foreign share of NZ govt securities rose in July.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners rose to 54.4 percent in July from 53.7 percent in June, the Reserve Bank said on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   July 1996	     June 1996	     July 1995</p>
<p>	     Value  Percent*    Value   Percent*    Value Percent*</p>
<p>T Bills     2917.4    44.8     3249.9    49.0     3827.4    59.1</p>
<p>Govt Bonds 11734.1    57.4    11121.9    55.2     6401.9    32.5</p>
<p>Total Govt Secs</p>
<p>	     14651.5    54.4    14371.8    53.7     10229.3   39.1</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds</p>
<p>10/96	   48.7    16.1	 48.7    16.1	  28.9    9.5</p>
<p>11/96	 1219.6    54.1     1159.9    50.4	 812.0   33.1</p>
<p>7/97	   963.9    49.1	921.5    47.0	 456.6   23.3</p>
<p>7/98	  1534.7    62.7     1571.1    64.2	 440.5   18.0</p>
<p>2/00	  1747.0    58.0     1454.0    48.3	 537.5   18.8</p>
<p>2/01	  1243.4    73.1     1024.3    64.0	   0.0    0.0</p>
<p>3/02	  1391.5    55.4     1395.7    55.6	 790.0   31.4</p>
<p>4/04	  1802.5    59.2     1895.0    62.3	1696.8   55.7</p>
<p>11/06	 1709.7    61.6     1615.1    60.3	 480.3   33.7</p>
<p>02/16	   73.1    22.3	 36.6    18.3	   0.0    0.0</p>
<p>Values are expressed in terms of NZ$million.</p>
<p>* Represents non-residential holdings as a percentage of total securities in hands of market excluding RBNZ/Treasury holdings.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
</text>
